==Hindi==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sa|hi}} {{term|एक|sc=Deva|lang=sa|tr=éka}} (or a closely related Old-Indo-Aryan language, through Prakrit), from {{etyl|iir-pro|hi}} {{m|iir-pro|*Haykas}} (compare Persian {{term|یک|tr=yek|lang=fa}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|hi}} {{m|ine-pro|*óynos|*(H)óykos|one, single}}.

===Numeral===
{{cardinalbox|hi|०|१|२|शून्य|दो|ord=पहला|sc=Deva}}
{{hi-num-card|tr=ek|ur=ایک}}

# {{context|cardinal|lang=hi}} [[one]]; 1

===Adjective===
{{hi-adj|tr=ek|ur=ایک}}

# [[one]]
# [[a]]
# [[sole]]
# [[only]]

